      ":question/id": "7b399190-4276-5387-b44b-b79a69255e59",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The minimum set is $a_{21}$ and $a_{43}$. Replace these 2 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 2, 3, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{21}$ would put the leading entry of row 2 in column 1, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 1. Restoring $a_{43}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 3, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. No set with fewer than 2 replacements satisfies both the leading-entry order and zero-row conditions.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero.",
